G.18 Summary of Key Architectural Invariants

```
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║                    CEDA ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS                              ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

  INVARIANT 1 — HIERARCHICAL LAYERING
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Layer i may only communicate with layers i-1 and i+1 directly.          │
  │ Cross-layer messages are routed through defined interfaces.             │
  │ Safety Plane (Layer 6) may interrupt ANY layer unconditionally.         │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  INVARIANT 2 — SAFETY PRECEDENCE
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ P_delivered ≤ P_safe  ∀ (r, t)                                         │
  │ S_safe(s) ≤ 0  is a hard constraint, never violated.                   │
  │ Shutdown latency < 5 ms is guaranteed by hardware, not software.        │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  INVARIANT 3 — ENERGY CONSERVATION
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ P_gen + P_grid − P_load − P_losses = dE_storage/dt                     │
  │ Σ_r P_del,r · (1/η_r) ≤ P_fabric                                       │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  INVARIANT 4 — AUTHENTICATED ENERGY
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ No power transfer without prior authentication.                        │
  │ Every energy address A is bound to a cryptographic identity ID_r.       │
  │ Replay attacks prevented by nonce-based challenge-response.            │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  INVARIANT 5 — MODE SELECTION OPTIMALITY
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ μ(A) = argmin_m { cost_m(A) : constraints_m(A) satisfied }             │
  │ Mode selection is deterministic given address and system state.        │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  INVARIANT 6 — STANDARDS SCOPE RESPECT
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ CEDA claims compliance ONLY within the frequency ranges and scope       │
  │ of the cited standards. No extrapolation beyond stated scope.          │
  │ CIED safety is handled OUTSIDE IEC/IEEE 63184:2025 by explicit logic.  │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  INVARIANT 7 — VIRTUALIZATION FRACTION PARAMETERIZATION
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ α* is NEVER asserted as a fixed number.                                │
  │ α* = f(P_th, d_th, η, S_safe, H, C, R) is always computed from inputs. │
  │ The dissertation reports α* as a function, not a constant.             │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  INVARIANT 8 — SCOPE LIMITATION HONESTY
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Cableless ≠ conductor-free.                                            │
  │ CEDA virtualizes terminal distribution, not backbone transport.        │
  │ High-power loads (>2 kW) and long-distance (>30 cm resonant) remain    │
  │ cabled. This is a physical constraint, not a design choice.            │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

